cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite both the associated article and this archived repository."
title: "Observed phage–host ranges in the infant gut"
abstract: >-
  Sequence data and host-assignment tables supporting the study of phage–bacteria
  interactions in the early-life gut microbiome. The repository contains 13,235
  phage contigs (>= 10 kb) recovered from 55 infant faecal sample-timepoints, the
  per-sample bacterial genomes (MAGs) they were mapped against, and the resulting
  observed phage–host associations across three reference sets (the HumGut
  reference database, self bacterial assemblies, and pooled infant-cohort
  assemblies). All participant identifiers have been anonymised.
type: dataset
